# LF in the repository, whatever the working tree looks like. This was written
# on Windows and every blob went in as CRLF, which meant the first contributor
# on Linux would have rewritten every line of every file they saved. Normalised
# once, deliberately, rather than a line at a time by accident.
* text=auto

# Byte for byte as captured from the machines that produced them: real ss,
# lsof, /proc and PowerShell output. Any line ending conversion would change
# the input the parsers are tested against, which is the whole point of them.
test/fixtures/** -text

*.png binary
*.tgz binary

# Drawn by assets/make-screenshot.mjs from the program's own rendering code.
# Marked so a redraw does not drown a review in one enormous diff, and kept
# byte for byte as written so that CI can redraw it and compare it exactly.
assets/screen.svg -text linguist-generated=true
assets/screen.png linguist-generated=true
